%%{init: {'theme': 'dark'}}%%
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> CREATED : Order Created\n(after payment success)

    CREATED --> PAYMENT_PENDING : Awaiting Payment\nConfirmation
    CREATED --> CANCELLED : Manual Cancel

    PAYMENT_PENDING --> CONFIRMED : Payment Successful\n(PaymentConfirmedEvent)
    PAYMENT_PENDING --> PAYMENT_FAILED : Payment Failed /\nTimeout

    PAYMENT_FAILED --> CANCELLED : Auto-cancel

    CONFIRMED --> PROCESSING : Warehouse picks order

    PROCESSING --> SHIPPED : Order dispatched

    SHIPPED --> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY : With courier

    OUT_FOR_DELIVERY --> DELIVERED : Customer received

    CANCELLED --> [*]
    DELIVERED --> [*]

    note right of PAYMENT_PENDING
        If Order Service crashes here,
        the PaymentConfirmedEvent in Kafka
        is retried when service recovers.
        Idempotency key prevents duplicate order.
    end note

    note right of CONFIRMED
        Inventory: reserved → sold
        Kafka: OrderConfirmedEvent emitted
        Triggers: Shipment + Notification
    end note
